infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What you are decides how you pin
  desc A library resolves with strangers; an application answers to no resolver
  compares
    - label Library — declare ranges
      children
        - label Resolved with strangers
          desc Your httpx must intersect every other package's in apps you never see
        - label Tested lower bound
          desc A floor you actually run CI against, not a guess
        - label Exclude known-bad only
          desc !=2.31.1 — no upper cap without a real incompatibility
        - label Caps shrink the feasible set
          desc Two unrelated caps can empty it; resolution fails or backtracks
    - label Application — lock everything
      children
        - label No one resolves against you
          desc The whole job: Tuesday's deploy equals Friday's
        - label Full resolved graph
          desc Every transitive dependency, exact version, recorded
        - label sha256 per artifact
          desc --require-hashes fails closed on a hijacked re-release
        - label Index becomes a non-input
          desc Fresh installs are byte-identical; upgrade by re-locking
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
